  "_commit": {
    "id": "aba2a772d08874f3ca4f0dde1302e4e0cf969602",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Config/roxygen2/version change from 8.1.0 to 8.1.1 in DESCRIPTION. That last change is from a roxygen run and isn't part of the fix.\n\nAccept the legacy \"full_res_image_pixels\" unit in the SFE coercion\n\nas(mase, \"SpatialFeatureExperiment\") failed with \"'arg' should be one of\n\"full_res_image_pixel\", \"micron\"\" for any MASE built from an SFE that\nstores its unit as \"full_res_image_pixels\", which is how older SFE\nobjects, including the SFEData example datasets, record it. The SFE\nconstructor only accepts the singular spelling, and the coercion passed\nthe stored value through unchanged.\n\nNormalize the legacy spelling both when the unit is stored in\nmetadata(mase) and when it is read back, so MASE objects written before\nthis fix also convert. Adds a regression test that round-trips an SFE\ncarrying the legacy unit and a MASE with the legacy spelling already\nstored.\n",
    "time": 1794767444
  },
